g\r\n- PSR-0 and composer support.\r\n- Simpler configuration and bootstrapping.\r\n- Improved configuration handling.\r\n- Improved bake.\r\n\r\nSee [the roadmap](http://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/wiki/3.0-roadmap) for more details.","creator":null,"open_issues":0,"closed_issues":2464,"state":"closed","created_at":"2013-10-11T20:56:23Z","updated_at":"2015-12-17T03:00:48Z","due_on":"2015-03-22T04:00:00Z","closed_at":"2015-03-23T01:02:41Z"},"comments":1,"created_at":"2014-08-20T06:21:37Z","updated_at":"2014-08-20T10:11:44Z","closed_at":"2014-08-20T10:11:44Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I came to this problem while using AuthComponent, I found that Auth's sessions never persisted.\nSeems to be caused by Session::renew(), as it fails to renew current session when no session was started previously, from current renew() implementation:\n\n``` php\nif (!$this->_hasSession() || $this->_isCli) {\n    return;\n}\n\n$params = session_get_cookie_params();\nsetcookie(\n    session_name(), '', time() - 42000,\n    $params['path'], $params['domain'],\n    $params['secure'], $params['httponly']\n);\nsession_regenerate_id(true);\n```\n\nI think session_regenerate_id(true) should be used only if a valid session id already exists:\n\n``` php\nif (session_id()) {\n  // rest of the logic\n}\n```\n\nPS: Actually 2.x implementation of this method includes this `if (...)` condition\n","closed_by":{"login":"lorenzo","id":37621,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NjIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37621?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo","html_url":"https://github.com/lorenzo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"